@startuml
title Hunter Ranch recreation: prove one hole, then expand
autonumber
actor Designer as D
participant "Official Course References" as R
participant "USGS Data Sources" as S
participant QGIS as Q
participant Blender as B
participant "Unreal Open Golf" as U

D -> R: Check scorecard, routing, photographs and drone tour
R --> D: Course references and hole identities
D -> S: Locate property; inspect DEM and imagery coverage
S --> D: Selected data, metadata and source terms
D -> Q: Load data; establish CRS, boundary and source records
Q -> Q: Reproject, crop and inspect terrain
D -> Q: Trace surfaces, routes and tee/green markers
Q --> D: Geographic master and Hole 1 export package
D -> B: Build terrain from height data; align reference overlay
D -> B: Refine green, bunkers and surface boundaries
B --> D: Terrain mesh, material slots and coordinate notes
D -> U: Import mesh; configure surfaces, collision, tee and cup
U --> D: Visual, dimensional and gameplay checks
loop Until first-hole checks pass
  alt Geographic alignment or source terrain problem
    D -> Q: Correct source preparation or layout
    Q --> D: Updated export with the same origin
    D -> B: Update terrain and aligned references
  else Local shape or boundary problem
    D -> B: Correct geometry or surface assignments
  end
  B --> D: Revised mesh
  D -> U: Reimport and repeat checks
  D -> U: Adjust gameplay setup if required
  U --> D: Validation results
end
loop Remaining holes, in manageable groups
  D -> Q: Verify routing and trace features
  Q --> D: Aligned source exports
  D -> B: Refine terrain and scenery
  B --> D: Course assets
  D -> U: Integrate and validate each hole
end
@enduml
